  m_Name: ReadMe
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  data:
    title: Custom Save And Autosave
    summary: A custom SaveFile subclass stores project state next to the base economy
      state, while a custom SaveAndLoad coalesces save-worthy events into queued writes
      and suppresses autosave during load.
    resourcePrefix: demo_customsave
    sections:
    - heading: Project setup
      body: DemoProjectSaveFile derives from SaveFile, captures project state in its
        constructor, and restores it after base.Load(). DemoCustomSaveAndLoad overrides
        Save and Load with SaveAndLoadSystem<DemoProjectSaveFile>, reapplies the clamped
        offline-time policy explicitly, and writes only after a save-worthy change.
    - heading: What to try
      body: Buy, produce, and travel from the Save-Worthy Events panel and watch source
        strings, same-frame suppression, and the coalesced write counter. Save a board
        version, disable autosave, change it again, then Load to see the saved project
        note and board version restored. Re-enable autosave to write pending changes,
        or activate the pre-granted Save-session automation boost, save, exit Play
        Mode, and re-enter to demonstrate offline profit without making the tracked
        Business auto-produce by default.
    - heading: Caveats
      body: Guard event-driven autosave while loading, treat the save-worthy callback
        as a dirty flag rather than a transaction log, and reconcile project-owned
        visuals from loaded holders after base state is restored. ProfitCalculator
        simulates only businesses eligible for automatic production, so the temporary
        automation boost must be active in the saved state for this manual Business
        to generate offline profit.
